\f1\fs22 Tony hailed a ground cab.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah hesitated when he opened the rusted door for her. \'91Let\'92s walk.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Walk?\'92 Tony reeled on his heels as if a prize-fighter clocked his chin. \'91Are you mad?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Possibly, Sarah considered, she was mad or at least traumatised. It was one thing feeling invincible, but exploding night clubs, rabid PAPER agents, and van crashes were still fearful. After the bombing, she\'92d spent almost two days in hospital while her burns and contusions cleared up.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The taxi was a jagged-tooth red-iron wolf coming to eat her, Little Red Cyber Hood. She shrank away from the hungry open door. \'91I know a place on the edge of The Ghetto. It\'92s dirty and seedy, so \'85 you\'92ll love it!\'92 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Let me guess.\'92 Tony felt clever. \'91It\'92s in the square with the statue of Zuckerburg the Redeemer?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Not too far from there, yes.\'92 Sarah felt less confident about her choice.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony burst out laughing. \'91That whole area is a tourist trap. It\'92s in the shade under a huge hover-copt pad, that is, if the sun ever shone on the Pale. All you Airbornes can buzz in with a minimum fuss. There\'92s even showers and dry-cleaners in the pad so you can wash the Cloudborne stink off before you leave. I\'92ll take you to where the Elvi roam, in the heart of the Ghetto. I hope you have no cuts. There\'92s a real chance of infection.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Sounds disgusting.\'92 Sarah felt good about rising to the challenge. \'91I think I can fight off infection.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony hailed another cab, rustier and clunkier than the one before. Sarah yanked the door open and jumped in.\
